{"type":"text","timestamp":1788474006022,"sessionID":"ses_f96a9ebceffeKmiM5H0EW3IjUw","part":{"id":"prt_0695b7f98001O3yB48wEDh1jbq","messageID":"msg_0695b6cba0011NiClGzdpDYyy1","sessionID":"ses_f96a9ebceffeKmiM5H0EW3IjUw","type":"text","text":"Done. JWK support for encoding is implemented across both APIs (matching upstream PyJWT PR #979):\n\n**`jwt/api_jws.py`** — `PyJWS.encode()` (jwt/api_jws.py:105)\n- `key` now accepts `PyJWK` alongside existing key types\n- `algorithm` defaults to `None` instead of `\"HS256\"`; resolution logic: PyJWK → `key.algorithm_name`, other keys → `\"HS256\"`, explicit values always win\n- Before signing, a `PyJWK`'s prepared key material (`key.key`) is extracted and passed through the algorithm's `prepare_key()`\n\n**`jwt/api_jwt.py`** — `PyJWT.encode()` (jwt/api_jwt.py:45)\n- Same signature update; algorithm resolution happens in the JWS layer it delegates to\n\n**Tests** (tests/test_api_jws.py)\n- Added `test_encode_default_algorithm` and `test_encode_with_jwk` (encodes/decodes round-trip using an `oct` JWK)\n- Updated the two `alg=none` tests to pass `algorithm=\"none\"` explicitly, since `None` now means \"choose based on key\"\n\n**CHANGELOG.rst** — added \"Add JWK support to JWT encode\" entry under Unreleased/Changed\n\nVerification: 273 tests pass (with `cryptography` installed, so RSA/EC paths exercised too) and `mypy jwt` is clean. Usage example:\n\n```python\njwk = PyJWK({\"kty\": \"oct\", \"alg\": \"HS384\", \"k\": \"c2VjcmV0\"})\njwt.encode({\"some\": \"payload\"}, jwk)  # alg inferred: HS384\njwt.encode({\"some\": \"payload\"}, \"secret\")  # defaults to HS256\n```","time":{"start":1788473999256,"end":1788474006016}}}
